  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>clusterdata</keyword>
  <short_description>Cluster observations from data.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>T = clusterdata(X, &apos;MaxClust&apos;, maxclust)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>T = clusterdata(X, &apos;Cutoff&apos;, cutoff, &apos;Criterion&apos;, &apos;distance&apos;)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>T = clusterdata(..., &apos;Linkage&apos;, method)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>T = clusterdata(..., &apos;Distance&apos;, metric)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>clusterdata</b> groups rows of <b>X</b> by building a hierarchical cluster tree and cutting it into clusters.</p>
    <p>This version supports the distance criterion with MaxClust or Cutoff. Linkage and distance options are passed to <b>linkage</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [0 0; 1 0; 0 2; 4 4];
T = clusterdata(X, 'MaxClust', 2)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
